Addr  Word  Source
------------------------------------------------------------
            ; prng.asm — hardware PRNG demo
            ; clk_div: 20
            ;
            ; Reads the hardware Galois LFSR (rtl/prng.v) into R7 on every CPU cycle
            ; using the IN instruction, then loops forever.
            ;
            ; The LFSR runs at the board clock rate (12 MHz), independent of the CPU
            ; clock (~11 Hz at clk_div=20).  Each IN therefore samples the LFSR at a
            ; different point in its 255-step sequence, producing values that look
            ; random to the program.
            ;
            ; Display: switch board to mode 1 (short button press) to see R7 on LEDs.
            ;
            ; Register use:
            ;   R7 = sampled PRNG value → drives LED display in mode 1
            ;
            ; This program runs forever — it never halts.
            
            loop:
0000  8E00          IN   R7         ; R7 = hardware PRNG value
0001  4000          JMP  loop       ; sample again next CPU cycle
